WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.307 --> 00:00:17.028
nights later the matron of the workhouse where Oliver was born was having tea.

2
00:00:18.148 --> 00:00:22.529
Outside the snow lay frozen in a hard, thick crust and the wind howled sharply.

3
00:00:23.469 --> 00:00:26.910
But everything was warm and cozy inside the room belonging to Mrs.

4
00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:32.112
Corney. The widow sat at a table in front of the cheerful fire and looked around with a

5
00:00:32.212 --> 00:00:33.312
self-satisfied air.

6
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.061
"Well," she said to herself.

7
00:00:36.082 --> 00:00:41.686
"We all have much to be grateful for, being indoors on a bitter night like this one."

8
00:00:42.747 --> 00:00:46.970
Mrs. Corney had just tasted her first cup of tea when she was disturbed by a rap on

9
00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:47.451
her door.

10
00:00:47.471 --> 00:00:49.933
"Come in," said Mrs.

11
00:00:49.993 --> 00:00:50.773
Corney sharply.

12
00:00:50.793 --> 00:00:53.776
"Some old woman is probably dying.

13
00:00:54.837 --> 00:00:56.758
They always die when I'm at meals.

14
00:00:57.799 --> 00:00:58.500
What's wrong?"

15
00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.742
"Nothing, ma'am, nothing," said a man's voice.

16
00:01:01.762 --> 00:01:03.564
"Dear me!"

17
00:01:03.936 --> 00:01:05.917
the matron exclaimed in a much sweeter tone.

18
00:01:05.938 --> 00:01:07.699
"Is that Mr.

19
00:01:07.799 --> 00:01:10.981
Bumble?" "At your service, ma'am."

20
00:01:12.022 --> 00:01:15.524
The parish officer was carrying his hat in one hand and a bundle in the other.

21
00:01:15.544 --> 00:01:17.726
"Bad weather, Mr.

22
00:01:17.766 --> 00:01:20.127
Bumble." "Bad indeed, ma'am.

23
00:01:21.128 --> 00:01:25.351
This very afternoon we gave away twenty loaves of bread and a cheese and a half, and still

24
00:01:25.391 --> 00:01:26.792
those paupers are not content."

25
00:01:26.812 --> 00:01:28.753
"Of course not.

26
00:01:29.814 --> 00:01:30.695
When would they be?"

27
00:01:31.075 --> 00:01:32.456
said the matron, sipping her tea.

28
00:01:33.564 --> 00:01:34.265
"When indeed."

29
00:01:35.265 --> 00:01:36.767
Mr. Bumble unpacked his bundle.

30
00:01:36.787 --> 00:01:40.409
"I brought the port wine that the board ordered for the infirmary."

31
00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:45.853
He placed the two bottles on top of a chest of drawers and folded up the handkerchief in

32
00:01:45.893 --> 00:01:46.874
which they had been wrapped.

33
00:01:47.855 --> 00:01:51.177
He put that in his pocket and picked up his hat as if preparing to go.

34
00:01:51.197 --> 00:01:54.540
"You'll have a very cold walk," said the matron.

35
00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:57.282
"The wind blows sharply tonight, ma'am."

36
00:01:58.343 --> 00:01:59.964
Mr. Bumble turned up his coat collar.

37
00:02:01.624 --> 00:02:03.345
"Would you stay and take a cup of tea?"

38
00:02:03.745 --> 00:02:04.805
she inquired shyly.

39
00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:09.226
Mr. Bumble instantly turned down his collar and took a seat before the fire.

40
00:02:10.246 --> 00:02:12.507
Mrs. Corney rose to get another cup and saucer.

41
00:02:13.627 --> 00:02:15.448
As she sat down, her eyes met Mr.

42
00:02:15.488 --> 00:02:16.808
Bumble's, and she blushed.

43
00:02:17.949 --> 00:02:18.629
"Sweet, Mr.

44
00:02:18.689 --> 00:02:20.969
Bumble?" she inquired, picking up the sugar.

45
00:02:20.989 --> 00:02:23.570
"Very sweet indeed, ma'am."

46
00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:25.871
He regarded her tenderly.

47
00:02:26.931 --> 00:02:29.652
As she handed him a cup of tea, he squeezed her little finger.

48
00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:31.541
They talked of Mrs.

49
00:02:31.621 --> 00:02:32.842
Corney's cat and kittens.

50
00:02:33.943 --> 00:02:35.484
They drank more tea, and Mr.

51
00:02:35.524 --> 00:02:38.347
Bumble edged his chair around the table until it touched Mrs.

52
00:02:38.407 --> 00:02:39.068
Corney's chair.

53
00:02:40.129 --> 00:02:45.153
The parish officer drank his last drop of tea, ate a piece of toast, and kissed the matron.

54
00:02:45.173 --> 00:02:47.255
"Mr. Bumble!"

55
00:02:47.675 --> 00:02:48.296
exclaimed Mrs.

56
00:02:48.376 --> 00:02:49.197
Corney in a whisper.

57
00:02:50.958 --> 00:02:53.641
She was so startled that she had quite lost her voice.

58
00:02:54.962 --> 00:02:57.024
"Mr. Bumble, I shall scream!"

59
00:02:58.048 --> 00:03:01.230
Mr. Bumble made no reply but put his arm around her waist.

60
00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:06.693
Mrs. Corney would have screamed, except just then there was a hasty knocking at the door.

61
00:03:07.733 --> 00:03:11.475
Mr. Bumble darted to the wine bottles and began dusting them with great energy.

62
00:03:11.495 --> 00:03:13.156
"Who's there?"

63
00:03:13.496 --> 00:03:15.938
Mrs. Corney demanded in her usual sharp voice.

64
00:03:17.038 --> 00:03:19.059
An old pauper woman put her head in at the door.

65
00:03:19.079 --> 00:03:23.262
"If you please, mistress, Old Sally is dying."

66
00:03:23.282 --> 00:03:25.783
"Well, what's that to me?"

67
00:03:26.223 --> 00:03:27.444
angrily demanded the matron.

68
00:03:28.572 --> 00:03:30.293
"I can't keep her alive, can I?"

69
00:03:30.313 --> 00:03:32.035
"No, mistress.

70
00:03:33.035 --> 00:03:34.737
She says she has something to tell you."

71
00:03:35.777 --> 00:03:36.998
With much annoyance, Mrs.

72
00:03:37.058 --> 00:03:39.580
Corney wrapped herself in a shawl and followed the woman.

73
00:03:41.341 --> 00:03:43.983
Sally was sitting up in bed when they arrived at her bedside.

74
00:03:44.003 --> 00:03:49.127
"You must lie down," said the pauper woman, helping Sally back onto her pillow.

75
00:03:49.147 --> 00:03:53.330
"Send her away," said Old Sally to Mrs.

76
00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:55.672
Corney. "Make haste."

77
00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:58.661
Mrs. Corney dismissed the pauper woman.

78
00:03:59.662 --> 00:04:02.523
Sally reached out a hand and pulled her down into a chair.

79
00:04:02.543 --> 00:04:06.065
"Now listen to me," said the dying woman.

80
00:04:06.085 --> 00:04:10.588
"In this very room I once nursed a pretty young creature.

81
00:04:11.708 --> 00:04:14.230
She gave birth to a boy and died.

82
00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:17.972
Let me think what was the year?"

83
00:04:17.992 --> 00:04:20.233
"Never mind the year.

84
00:04:21.214 --> 00:04:21.914
What about her?"

85
00:04:21.934 --> 00:04:24.916
"She was barely dead when I stole it.

86
00:04:25.856 --> 00:04:27.136
The only thing she had.

87
00:04:27.156 --> 00:04:28.957
A necklace.

88
00:04:30.117 --> 00:04:32.138
Gold. Pure gold.

89
00:04:33.258 --> 00:04:37.780
She could have sold it for food or clothing, but she kept it safe around her neck."

90
00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.060
"Gold!" Mrs.

91
00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.061
Corney bent eagerly over the dying woman.

92
00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:44.341
"Go on.

93
00:04:45.342 --> 00:04:46.282
What happened to it?"

94
00:04:46.302 --> 00:04:50.243
"And the boy "What boy?"

95
00:04:50.263 --> 00:04:52.564
"They named him Oliver.

96
00:04:53.536 --> 00:04:55.698
He grew to look so like his mother.

97
00:04:56.699 --> 00:04:57.480
Poor girl.

98
00:04:58.641 --> 00:05:00.943
I always thought of her whenever I saw him."

99
00:05:00.963 --> 00:05:02.924
"But the necklace.

100
00:05:03.965 --> 00:05:05.367
What did you do with the necklace?"

101
00:05:06.508 --> 00:05:09.090
Sally pulled the matron closer and whispered something.

102
00:05:10.011 --> 00:05:12.072
Then she closed her eyes and died.

103
00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:14.675
Mrs. Corney quickly left the room.

104
00:05:14.695 --> 00:05:17.958
"She had nothing to tell me after all," Mrs.

105
00:05:18.018 --> 00:05:20.400
Corney said to the pauper woman, who was waiting in the hall.

106
00:05:21.448 --> 00:05:22.189
Meanwhile Mr.

107
00:05:22.229 --> 00:05:23.991
Bumble had been left by himself in Mrs.

108
00:05:24.051 --> 00:05:24.651
Corney's room.

109
00:05:25.672 --> 00:05:30.997
He opened the closet, counted the teaspoons, weighed the sugar tongs in his hand, and inspected a milk

110
00:05:31.057 --> 00:05:32.979
pot to be sure it was genuine silver.

111
00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:38.164
Trying to decide how much she was worth, he then sat down to take an inventory of the

112
00:05:38.224 --> 00:05:41.107
furniture. Still Mrs.

113
00:05:41.187 --> 00:05:42.248
Corney did not return.

114
00:05:43.269 --> 00:05:46.472
He recounted the teaspoons and double-checked the condition of the furniture.

115
00:05:47.488 --> 00:05:50.629
Perhaps, he thought, he should have a quick glance through the contents of Mrs.

116
00:05:50.669 --> 00:05:51.910
Corney's chest of drawers.

117
00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:55.831
Mr. Bumble listened at the keyhole to make sure no one was coming.

118
00:05:56.932 --> 00:05:58.813
Then he opened the three long drawers.

119
00:05:59.933 --> 00:06:04.435
Among the various garments of good fashion and texture, he found a small padlocked box.

120
00:06:05.575 --> 00:06:10.037
Mr. Bumble shook the box and it gave forth a pleasant sound like the clinking of coins.

121
00:06:11.138 --> 00:06:13.779
Mr. Bumble returned with a stately walk to the fireplace.

122
00:06:13.799 --> 00:06:15.499
"I'll do it!"

123
00:06:15.859 --> 00:06:16.820
he declared to himself.

124
00:06:17.876 --> 00:06:18.597
Just then Mrs.

125
00:06:18.657 --> 00:06:21.058
Corney burst into the room in a state of agitation.

126
00:06:21.078 --> 00:06:22.679
"What's wrong?"

127
00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:24.441
asked the parish officer in alarm.

128
00:06:24.461 --> 00:06:28.083
"Oh, nothing, nothing," she said breathlessly.

129
00:06:28.103 --> 00:06:31.045
"Tea! I must have more tea."

130
00:06:32.786 --> 00:06:35.288
Mr. Bumble bustled about, making another pot of tea.

131
00:06:36.289 --> 00:06:37.990
He watched with concern as Mrs.

132
00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:39.391
Corney drank the hot liquid.

133
00:06:40.431 --> 00:06:42.513
The tea had a settling effect upon her.

134
00:06:42.533 --> 00:06:46.095
"You know the master of the workhouse is dying, my dear?"

135
00:06:46.436 --> 00:06:46.836
he said.

136
00:06:47.892 --> 00:06:53.574
"Yes." "He may not live another week, and his death will open up a vacancy that perhaps I

137
00:06:53.654 --> 00:06:54.354
might fill."

138
00:06:55.434 --> 00:06:57.235
Mr. Bumble suddenly grasped her hands.

139
00:06:57.255 --> 00:06:58.855
"Oh, Mrs.

140
00:06:58.935 --> 00:07:01.176
Corney, what a prospect this opens!

141
00:07:02.196 --> 00:07:04.456
What an opportunity for a joining of our hearts!

142
00:07:05.477 --> 00:07:06.697
Will you say yes to me?"

143
00:07:07.777 --> 00:07:11.998
"Yes!" And with that the happy couple was engaged to be married.

144
00:07:12.979 --> 00:07:13.399
But Mr.

145
00:07:13.459 --> 00:07:14.859
Bumble had one more question.

146
00:07:14.879 --> 00:07:17.600
"What was it that agitated you so?"

147
00:07:18.736 --> 00:07:20.479
"Nothing in particular," Mrs.

148
00:07:20.539 --> 00:07:21.641
Corney said evasively.

149
00:07:21.661 --> 00:07:25.506
"I'll tell you sometime after we're married, dear."
